      "title": "Employment Posting:10-Month Laboratory Instructor (Permanent), School of Nursing",
      "description": "10-Month Laboratory Instructor (Permanent), School of Nursing Skip to main content Top menu Information for Future Students Current Students Indigenous Initiatives International Students Alumni Donors Community Faculty and Staff MyNipissing Need Support? Search Search Main navigation Academics Academics submenu Academics submenu Academic Services Academic Services submenu Academic Programs Office of the Registrar Academic Advising Academic Calendar Academic Faculties Academic Faculties submenu Faculty of Arts and Science Faculty of Education and Professional Studies School of Graduate Studies Teaching & Learning Teaching & Learning submenu Centre for Teaching and Learning Extended Learning AQ and ABQ Courses Life at NU Life at NU submenu Life at NU submenu Living at NU Living at NU submenu Residence Meal Plans and Dining on Campus Off-Campus Living Campus Life & Community Campus Life & Community submenu Athletics Alumni Lakers Shop Campus Shop What's Happening at NU What's Happening at NU submenu Student Union (NUSU) Events News Student Supports Student Supports submenu Student Supports submenu Academic Supports Academic Supports submenu Academic Support Resources Academic Success Program Academic Integrity Student Learning and Transitions Student Development & Transitions Student Development & Transitions submenu Career Development and Education Dave Marshall Leadership Awards Orientation Mature & Transfer Student Supports Record of Student Development Belonging, Health & Wellbeing Belonging, Health & Wellbeing submenu Access and Belonging Accessibility Services Mental Health and Wellbeing Sexual Violence Supports Health Services and Health Plan Student Services Student Services submenu Student Financial Services Technology Services Office of Indigenous Initiatives Office of Indigenous Initiatives submenu Indigenous Student Success Indigenous Mentorship NUICE Indigenous Student Self-Identification International Student Support International Student Support submenu Study Abroad and Exchange Students International Student Mentorship Program Research Research submenu Research submenu Discover Research at Nipissing Discover Research at Nipissing submenu Canada Research Chairs Program Research Directory Research Centres Research Facilities & Groups News and Events Research Support Research Support submenu Research Data Management Safeguarding Your Research Funding Your Research Research Software Research Quick Links Responsible Research Responsible Research submenu Research Ethics Research Policies Intellectual Property and Commercialization Strategic Research Plan Northern and Rural Innovation Cluster Library Library submenu Library submenu Library Resources Library Resources submenu Archives and Special Collections Borrow from Other Libraries Government Resources Search Resources Understanding Archival Records Services Services submenu Library Services Printing in the Library Library Donations Connect Connect submenu Library Hours Library Team Liaison Librarians About Us About Us submenu About Us submenu Leadership & Administration Leadership & Administration submenu Office of the President Provost and Vice-President, Academic Vice-President, Finance and Administration Assistant Vice-President, Students Governance Campus & Community Campus & Community submenu Our Campus Discover North Bay Campus Map Open House Campus Tours Land Acknowledgement Engage with Nipissing Engage with Nipissing submenu Become a Student Careers Donate Events News Contact Donate Apply Breadcrumb Home Careers All Employment Postings 10-Month Laboratory Instructor (Permanent), School of Nursing Employment Posting: 10-Month Laboratory Instructor (Permanent), School of Nursing Job Advertisement - 10m Laboratory Instructor, School of Nursing PDF · 178 KB View PDF (PDF, opens in a new window) Download Employment Type: Full-time Faculty Closing Date: October 16, 2026 Position Posted: 1 day ago School of Nursing 10-Month Permanent Laboratory Instructor Simulationist The School of Nursing in the Faculty of Education and Professional Studies at Nipissing University invites applications for a 10-month permanent Laboratory Instructor (Simulationist). The successful candidate will ideally commence by January 1, 2027, or as soon as possible, and will support the integration of theory and clinical knowledge through experiential, simulation-based learning activities in the Simulation Centre . This position is located in North Bay, Ontario. This is an exciting opportunity to be part of the team to continue developing Nipissing University’s George and Helen Vari Simulation Centre with an initial concentrated focus on supporting Nursing theory and clinical courses with plans to expand support to other disciplines (e.g., Education, Social Work). The School of Nursing is one of the largest Schools in Nipissing University. The School focuses on quality undergraduate teaching and research while planning the establishment of a graduate program for nurses. The School of Nursing has a strong reputation for being student-centered and providing students with rich practice-based learning opportunities. The successful candidate will work collaboratively with faculty colleagues, other instructors in the Simulation Centre, support staff, administrators, and students to support the delivery and ongoing development of high-quality, experiential simulation-based learning. The successful candidate will have: A minimum of a Baccalaureate degree in nursing is required. A minimum of two years clinical experience is required. Current registration as a Registered Nurse with the College of Nurses of Ontario (CNO) with no restrictions to practice is required. Experience in simulation-based education is preferred. A simulation education credential would be considered an asset. A master’s degree in nursing or a health-related discipline is considered an asset. If you are excited about this position and meet most, but not all, of the listed qualifications, please still consider applying. We recognize that no one person might have every qualification in this job ad. The Simulationist’s responsibilities include simulation and laboratory instruction (e.g., high fidelity, immersive, virtual) and assessment, and design of simulation activities to support the learning outcomes of clinical and theory-based courses addressing the needs of the various of the Schools which utilize the George and Helen Vari Simulation Centre. The successful candidate will deliver and assess lab learning experiences connected to courses (e.g., instruction and demonstration of nursing skills); incorporate best practice (including design of simulation scenarios, pre-briefing and debriefing) and evidenced-based research in simulation program development with a focus on supporting concept based learning; design/co-design in collaboration with course instructors simulations, utilize various types of simulation fidelity and be familiar with computer technology; act as a resource person for independent student practice; and support hosting of internal and external partners doing simulation activities within the Centre. Our campus is located at 100 College Dr, North Bay, ON P1B 8L7. Based on the Collective Agreement, the annual salary for this role will range from $47,581 to $76,743, plus employee benefits and pension plan as per the collective agreement. The annual salary will correspond with qualifications, skills and level of experience and will follow the Nipissing University Faculty Association (NUFA) Full-time Academic Staff Bargaining Unit Collective Agreement . Nipissing University is located in the City of North Bay, Ontario (population 55,000), in the territory of the Robinson-Huron Treaty of 1850 and the Nipissing First Nation Traditional Territory and the traditional territory of the Anishinabek. Situated between Lake Nipissing and Trout Lake, and surrounded by pristine Canadian Shield Forest, our campus is a comfortable three-and-a-half-hour drive from either Toronto or Ottawa. North Bay is a growing city with a vibrant arts community, ample amenities, and countless opportunities for outdoor activities. Nipissing University is known for its excellence in teacher education, arts, science, and a range of professional programs. The School of Graduate Studies includes programs in history, sociology, education, environmental science/studies, kinesiology, and mathematics. In “ Pathways: Our Commitments to Water, Land, and People ”, Nipissing University has committed to fulfilling our responsibility to truth and reconciliation; nurturing our relationship with water, land and place; embodying harmony and care; inspiring growth and development; building sustainable futures; and, celebrating who we are. Nipissing’s renowned focus on student success and experience has translated into top rankings nationally in the areas of student support, student experience, faculty, and residences as a primarily undergraduate institution. An academic environment that provides close student-faculty interaction, innovative approaches to learning, and a strong research culture is an enduring strength of Nipissing. Access and equity continue to be longstanding priorities, providing interventions and support for students who might not otherwise participate in postsecondary education. Nipissing welcomes a number of first-generation students, as well as students with disabilities with focused supports. Nipissing’s faculty and staff are committed to decolonization and reconciliation and provide a supportive environment for Indigenous students enrolled at the University. Our campus is located in a region home to 7,000 First Nations, Métis, and Inuit residents, many of whom choose to study at Nipissing University. As a public university located on the traditional territory of Nipissing First Nation and on the lands within the Robinson-Huron Treaty of 1850, Nipissing University is bound to advance knowledge and be a good guest on this land. Interested candidates should submit a cover letter highlighting their relevant experience, including: Simulation experience, particularly hands-on simulation, in practice and/or education; Experience with a concept-based curriculum, if applicable; Experience using technology in teaching and/or simulation; Teaching experience, including experience in a post-secondary institution; and Clinical or other relevant professional experience. Please also include a curriculum vitae and the names and contact information for three referees. Please submit the completed application by 4:00pm on Friday October 16, 2026. Review of applications will commence Monday October 19, 2026, and will continue to be accepted and reviewed until the position is filled. Applicants should include a statement confirming their eligibility to work in Canada. These materials should be sent in one PDF document to careers@nipissingu.ca . Nipissing University is committed to employment equity and strongly encourages applications, which may include self-identification in a cover letter from Indigenous peoples, women, persons with disabilities, persons who identify as 2SLGBTQI+ and racialized minorities. Nipissing University must gather information from applicants to determine eligibility to work in Canada.  Please include a statement in your application to identify whether you are a Canadian Citizen, Permanent Resident or are otherwise legally eligible to work in Canada. Nipissing University will provide accommodation to ensure barrier-free employment in accordance with the Ontario Human Rights Code and the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act. You can request accommodation at any stage of the hiring process. If you require an accommodation, please contact Human Resources at access@nipissingu.ca . In compliance with Ontario's Employment Standards Act, this posting includes the expected compensation range and indicates that AI is not used in our hiring process. This position is for an existing vacancy at Nipissing University. The search committee would like to thank all applicants for their interest in Nipissing University. Please note that only those candidates invited for an interview will be contacted. Working at Nipissing Competitive Compensation Benefits, Pensions, Salary Learn more Health and Wellness Gym membership, Pickleball, Yoga Learn more Career Development Tuition subsidy, Professional development funds Learn more Why North Bay? North Bay is a dazzling jewel nestled between two of Northeastern Ontario’s most breathtaking lakes and enveloped by lush, expansive forests. Just 3.5 hours north of Toronto and 4 hours west of Ottawa, this vibrant city seamlessly blends modern sophistication with a deep appreciation for nature, art, and culture. Whether you're drawn to its natural wonders, lively cultural scene, or unique local charm, North Bay has a wealth of experiences waiting to captivate you! Discover North Bay Nipissing University 100 College Drive, Box 5002, North Bay, ON, Canada  P1B 8L7 705-474-3450 Footer CONNECT Careers Contact Directory Events News Map HELPFUL LINKS Blackboard Health & Safety Help Desk Ticket Request Student Support Student Financial Services WebAdvisor LEGAL & ACCESSIBILITY Accessibility Copyright Disclaimer Governance Policies and Guidelines Website Privacy Nipissing University sits on the territory of Nipissing First Nation, the territory of the Anishnabek, within lands protected by the Robinson Huron Treaty of 1850. We are grateful to be able to live and learn on these lands with all our relations. © Nipissing University 2026 This site uses cookies 🍪 We use cookies and similar technologies to support site functionality, understand how visitors use our website, and personalize content and advertising. OK Decline"
